From: Agent
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Force b_max=1 for SPL in DM probe

When u-boot,dm-spl is set, SPL uses sunxi_mmc_probe() instead of sunxi_mmc_init().
Because CMD18 (multi-block reads) hangs the controller in PIO mode without DMA,
we must force single-block reads (b_max = 1) for the eMMC in SPL when using DM.

---
 drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
@@ -717,6 +717,12 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 		cfg->f_max = 12000000;
 	}
 
+#if defined(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD) || defined(CONFIG_XPL_BUILD)
+	if (priv->mmc_no == 2) {
+		cfg->b_max = 1;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	ret = clk_get_by_name(dev, "ahb", &gate_clk);
 	if (!ret)
 		clk_enable(&gate_clk);
